<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belagavi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Belgaum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Belagavi, known as Belgaum until 2014, is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a>. Its fort dates from the 13th century, and the town was held in turn by the Bahmani and Adil Shahi sultans, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and the British. The city and its district have a large Marathi-speaking population, and their status has been disputed between Karnataka and Maharashtra since 1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belagavi.jpg" alt="Belagavi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shubham S. Sankannavar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kamal_Basti_view,_Belgaum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
